{
 "comment": "loans_interest, bridge#802, a firm: a loan taken in cash after a repayment made once interest was credited, under the limit on the walked principal and over it on principal plus the interest not yet paid, is listed as not computed (First Loan; Same Loan, interest and repayment on one day). Controls: no interest (Plain Loan), interest credited only after the repayment (Late Loan), the principal alone over the limit (Over Loan), and the First shape taken by bank (Bank Loan, listed but not a possible s.269SS), and an interest reversal before any interest is credited, which does not count as interest credited (Reversed Loan); loans taken after interest with no repayment (Taken Loan); a repayment before the first interest credited (Before Loan); the principal walk going below zero, where the later cash loan is R2's two-walks record, checked before this one (Walks Loan); and a repayment whose GUID sorts before the interest credit on the same day, listed (Order Loan).",
